course: dictionary
lesson: 9874
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Tablet is a good example. The words around it tell you which meaning to choose. In «Your dose depends on your age and weight», a dose is the amount of medicine you take, so a tablet here is a small pill you swallow.
explain: Now read this: «Noah's tablet got so hot from a long game that it switched itself off.» A tablet that plays games is a thin, flat computer with a touch screen. Long game, hot and switched off are the clues. They point to a device, not medicine.
explain: Tablet can also mean a flat piece of stone or clay with writing on it, used long ago. Or a tablet of soap is just a bar of soap. To check your meaning, put it into the sentence in place of the word and see if it still makes sense.
fact: A tablet can mean a small pill that you swallow as medicine.
fact: A tablet can mean a thin, flat computer with a touch screen.
fact: A tablet can mean a flat piece of stone or clay with writing on it, used long ago.
fact: A tablet of soap is a bar of soap.
fact: Only take tablets that a parent or doctor gives you, in the right amount, and keep them out of reach of small children, because tablets can look like sweets.
exercise: «Your dose depends on your age and weight.» What does tablet mean here? | *A small pill you swallow as medicine | A bar of soap | A flat piece of clay with writing on it | A thin, flat computer
exercise: «Noah's tablet got so hot from a long game that it switched itself off.» What does tablet mean here? | A bar of soap | *A thin, flat computer with a touch screen | A stone with writing on it | A small pill you swallow
exercise: Why should you keep tablets out of reach of small children? | Because they can be used as computers | *Because they can look like sweets | Because they are heavy | Because they are made of clay
test: «A pill box with the days of the week helps someone see whether today's tablets have been taken.» What does tablets mean here? | A computer with a touch screen | *Small pills you swallow | A bar of soap | A flat piece of stone
test: The ancient Sumerians wrote on clay tablets. What is a clay tablet? | *A flat piece of clay with writing on it | A bar of soap | A small pill you swallow | A thin computer with a touch screen
exam: In «Your dose depends on your age and weight», which word is the best clue that tablet means medicine? | Your | *Dose | sister's | little
